// Named zones, compiled from the IANA release this package carries.
//
// The data is the release's own compendium — the `Rule`, `Zone` and `Link` lines
// its editors maintain — so the reader here is the small language `zic` compiles:
// a zone is a run of stretches of time, each with a standard offset, a rule set (or
// one fixed amount of saving) and a format for the abbreviation, and each ending
// where the next begins.
//
// A separate package because the database is 105 kB of text that most callers do
// not need: one that formats an HTTP date carries the calendar, one that answers
// "what time is it in São Paulo" carries this as well.
import {
  "moonbitstack/moondate",
  "moonbitstack/moondate/zone",
}
